help->install new software use below link install it 
https://cucumber.github.io/cucumber-eclipse-update-site-snapshot/

2] Cretae Maven Project 

3] Add 3 dependency for cucumber and other aslo selenium and testng 
for this refer pom.xml of this project 

4] Ceate Feature file 


Folder Structure 

1] Under Src/Test Create Frist pkg for the Stepdef
2] Under Src/Test Create Second pkg for the TestRunner
3] Under SRC/Resources Create Feature file for your testing 



For execution :-

1]Create Feature File :- use proper syntax 

When repative pre condition you need [For e.g open application ]
Use Background Tag name 
Background: 
Given open xyz application 

2]For Stepdef Run your feature file there you will get the unimplemented method declartion part 
copy and create Normal java class and paste remove body of method and start your scription part 



3] For test runner create simple java class use below annotation 

@RunWith(Cucumber.class)
@CucumberOptions(features="src/test/resources/FeatureFile/googleTest.feature",
                 glue="Com.StepDef")
                 
                 
Feature contains feature file path 
glue contains step def pkg name [only pkg name ]     



Tags in Cucumber :-

And operator not worked in cucumber tags use OR 
IF Multiple test cases not want to run add common tag name to that scenario [e.g @ignore]

tags="@homepage" --------for single scenario run 
tags="@all" -------------for all test cases run
tags="@homepage or @sellpage or @mxpage"---- specific test cases to run 
tags="not @homepage" ----------------------Expect homepage rel all run 
tags= "not @ignore"  -------------------------Skip multiple secnario use same tag name for all test cses use this sysntax


DataTable Provider in Cucumber :-

OpenCart application example 

used to methods here 
1] key value pair = asmap ()  method 
2]Just value = cells() method 

ASMAP ():-
 * For this method first remove import statement and add above of class name 
 * Second change method variable name 
 * We are passing data through the Key value pair
 * That is the reason we are using a Map 
 * asmap() method used to get data in key value pair  
 
 @asmap
  Scenario: Test Register Functionality
    Given open the OpenCart application
    When user enter valid feilds
      | fname | lname | email              | telephone  | password  | cpassword |
      | sanvi | kadam | sanvi192@gmail.com | 7898096545 | abc@sanvi | abc@sanvi |
    When user click on radio button
    When user clcik on the privacy checkbox
    When user clcik on Continue  button
    Then user should able to regester and get valid message

Cells():-
     *For this method first remove import statement and add above of class name 
     * Second change method variable name 
	 * Here we are using normal list bcz we have only one list of only key 
	 * using method cell

@cells
  Scenario: Test Login Functionality
    Given open cart application login page
    When user enter valid credentails
      | sanvi112@gmail.com | abc@sanvi |
    When user click on the login button of login page
    Then user should able to login account page

DataDriven Testing :-  Multiple inputs testing for single senario 

User senario Outline keyword for this 
Write normal feature file user input take this e.g
"<username>" and "<password>"

for test data use below syantx

Examples :

 	| username | password |
      | Admin    | admin123 |
      | pooja    | test123  |
      | Admin    | admin123 |
      | Abhay    | test123  |

Hooks :- Hooks means the the Certain rulles like annotations in TESTNG 

In Cucumber we have only two hooks 
a]@before- Before will run before every scenario
b]@after -After will run After every scenario


Hokks always in differnt pkg of framework 
to implement this use utility - Browser provider 

Steps :-

1] create a seperate pkg for utility create BrowserProvider 
  - use ThreadLocal class and create method setdriver get driver 
2] Create another pkg for hooks create class hooks 
  - create setup(@before) and tear_down(@after) method 
  - setup browser here in setup & quite in tear_down
  e.g 	driver=	BrowserProvider.setdriver("edge"); ---Browser setup
3] Update your step def class 
   WebDriver driver=BrowserProvider.getdriver();
  Comment your driver launch statement
4] Update your runner file as follwed below syntax 

@RunWith(Cucumber.class)
@CucumberOptions(features= "src\\test\\resources\\FeatureFile\\SwagLab.feature" ,
         glue={"Com.StepDef" ,"Com.apphooks"},
         publish=true)

-Add your hooks pkg name in glue 

Reporting :-
1] Simple reporting user publish = true in runner file 

@RunWith(Cucumber.class)
@CucumberOptions(features= "src\\test\\resources\\FeatureFile\\OpenCart.feature" ,
         glue="Com.StepDef" ,
         publish=true) 

2] ExtenT Reporting :-

1]Add dependency 

	<dependency>
			<groupId>tech.grasshopper</groupId>
			<artifactId>extentreports-cucumber7-adapter</artifactId>
			<version>1.12.0</version>
		</dependency>
		
2]Add plugin in in Runner file 

plugin={"com.aventstack.extentreports.cucumber.adapter.ExtentCucumberAdapter:"}


3]Add extent.properties file in src/test/ resources 

extent.properties ---this will define the all properties of your report

extent.reporter.spark.out=HtmlReport/SparkReport/Spark.html

screenshot.dir=Screenshots/
screenshot.rel.path=../Screenshots/

extent.reporter.spark.start=true
extent.reporter.pdf.start=true
extent.reporter.pdf.out=HtmlReport/PdfReport/ExtentPdf.pdf

extent.reporter.html.start=true
extent.reporter.html.out=test-output/HtmlReport/ExtentHtml.html

basefolder.name=HtmlReport
basefolder.datetimepattern=d-MMM-YY HH-mm-ss

systeminfo.os=windows


